It is Sunday morning and we have a lot of time.
Bruno and I are relaxing in the living room.
I take his favourite toy out of Sabine's bag.
Bruno sees it and jumps up immediately.
I throw the toy across the flat.
"Fetch it!" I call out happily.
The little dog runs quickly to the toy.
He takes it in his mouth and brings it back to me.
"Good boy, Bruno!" I say.
I praise him and stroke his head.
As a reward, I give him a little treat.
He eats the treat and looks at me expectantly.
We play for almost half an hour.
I throw the toy again and again.
Every time I call again: "Fetch it!"
Bruno fetches it and brings it back like a good boy.
Afterwards he is quite tired.
He is allowed to sleep on the rug now.
